{
  "dom_id": "step-q82660",
  "name": "Question 19",
  "problem": "$\\,$ **If** I am not sleeping, **then** I am awake.\n\nWhich of the following statements are equivalent to the conditional statement above?\n\nI. If I am not awake, then I am sleeping.\n\nII. If I am sleeping, then I am not awake.\n\nIII. If I am awake, then I am not sleeping.",
  "worked_solution": "Let's recall the following facts:\n\n- The contrapositive is logically equivalent to the original statement.\n\n- The inverse and the converse are logically equivalent to each other, but not to the original statement.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14252532/assets/0deb19675402bf931111bb80cb616682aac08491b5cd3e1ab5812da05b6df8a8.png)\n\nSo, we are looking for the contrapositive.\n\n- Statement I is the contrapositive. $\\,✓$\n\n- Statement II is the inverse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement III is the converse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
